WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.146
An agent has no hire date
and no separation date,

2
00:00:03.146 --> 00:00:06.400
so its lifecycle has to hang
from a person who does.

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.898
Agent ID separates the owner,
who manages credentials,

4
00:00:09.898 --> 00:00:13.863
from the sponsor, who's accountable
for purpose and lifecycle.

5
00:00:13.863 --> 00:00:17.713
Left to defaults, the sponsor is
just whoever built the agent.

6
00:00:17.713 --> 00:00:22.666
The program decides instead: the sponsor
is a federal employee mastered in HR, a

7
00:00:22.666 --> 00:00:27.849
small group of stewards is the backup, and
the technical owner is never the sponsor.

8
00:00:27.849 --> 00:00:30.062
The lifecycle then follows that person.

9
00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:34.176
When the sponsor moves or leaves,
the HR event triggers a transfer,

10
00:00:34.176 --> 00:00:38.824
and the new sponsor has a short window
to confirm the agent is still needed.

11
00:00:38.824 --> 00:00:42.800
Access comes with end dates, so a
sponsor who does nothing removes it.

12
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:47.488
And an orphaned agent is disabled by
a person, never by an automatic rule.

13
00:00:47.488 --> 00:00:49.940
Next, credentials and privilege.
